@startuml
title stm — Event
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> Draft : create (UC15)

state Draft : editable (UC16)\nautosave
state Published : editable live (UC16)\n"Updated on" when schedule changes
state Cancelled : read-only (E1)\npublic banner + reason
state Archived : read-only (E1)\n"Past event"

Draft --> Published : publish (UC18)\n[required fields, verified email,\nfuture start (E2)]
Draft --> [*] : delete draft (UC20)
Draft --> [*] : untouched 12 months (S2)
Published --> Cancelled : cancel (UC19)\n[explicit confirmation]
Published --> Cancelled : association closed (UC8)\n[upcoming]
Published --> Archived : end passed\n(scheduled job)
Cancelled --> Archived : end passed\n(scheduled job)

state "Moderation overlay (orthogonal)" as Overlay {
  state Visible
  state Hidden : public 410, out of agenda and API
  [*] --> Visible
  Visible --> Hidden : hide (UC29)
  Hidden --> Visible : restore (UC32)
}
note right of Overlay
  Applies to Published, Cancelled and Archived.
  Hiding never changes the lifecycle state, so restoring
  returns the event exactly where it was.
  An association suspension hides its events the same way
  without touching their state.
end note
@enduml
